  <article>
    <h1>My Projects</h1>
    <p>
      Here is a showcase of the applications I have built and the open-source
      contributions I have made. They reflect my passion for backend
      architecture, accessibility (A11y), and social impact.
    </p>

    <section class="project-card" aria-labelledby="project-motamayezoon">
      <h2 id="project-motamayezoon">Motamayezoon Library API</h2>
      <p>
        <strong class="tech-label">Technologies:</strong> Node.js, Express, MongoDB, Mongoose, Joi,
        JWT, Mocha/Chai, Supertest, Swagger/OpenAPI, Cloudflare R2.
      </p>
      <p>
        A backend API designed to support the Motamayezoon team in their
        mission to convert accessible reading materials for blind and visually
        impaired users. The API manages book uploads, categorizes resources, and
        links them with book series. It supports three formats:
        <strong>KFX, EPUB, and AZW3</strong>, allowing users to easily download
        clean, well-formatted materials tailored for screen readers.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>33 REST endpoints</b> across 5 resources, with Joi validation on incoming requests.</li>
        <li><b>147 automated tests</b> (Mocha/Chai and Supertest) covering authentication, CRUD operations, permissions, and input validation.</li>
        <li>JWT authentication with role-based access control (user, uploader, admin), and protection against NoSQL injection, XSS, and parameter pollution.</li>
        <li>S3-compatible file storage, first DigitalOcean Spaces and then Cloudflare R2, and API documentation with Swagger/OpenAPI.</li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="link-list">
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/bassem-krayem/motamyezon_for_text_books_v2"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Source Code on GitHub<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="project-card" aria-labelledby="open-source">
      <h2 id="open-source">Open Source Contributions</h2>
      <p>
        <strong class="tech-label">Both merged upstream:</strong>
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <b>freeCodeCamp:</b> I found an accessibility bug in the Python
          terminal: screen readers received only the last line of output,
          because each print replaced the previous text. I fixed it so every
          printed line is added as its own paragraph (TypeScript/React), and
          tested it with my screen reader. Merged in October 2026.
          <a href="https://github.com/freeCodeCamp/freeCodeCamp/pull/70413" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View pull request #70413<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Cloudflare Docs:</b> while reading the R2 documentation to move
          Motamayezoon's file storage to Cloudflare R2, I found and fixed a typo
          in the public buckets guide. My first open-source contribution, merged
          in September 2026.
          <a href="https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflare-docs/pull/33703" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View pull request #33703<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

